course: dictionary
lesson: 9672
title: Successful: achieving your goal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Successful means you achieved what you wanted or tried to do. When something works out the way you planned, it is successful. Look at the words around it to be sure which meaning the writer means.
explain: «Dyslexia is a difference that makes reading and spelling harder; it has nothing to do with being clever, and many very successful people have it.» Here successful means having done well in life, work or business. The clue is the word people, and the idea of doing well over time.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Many people who did very well in life have it» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Successful can also describe a plan, a test or an experiment that works as planned.
fact: Successful means achieving what you wanted or tried to do.
fact: Successful can also mean having done well in life, work or business.
fact: A successful experiment gives the result you tested for.
fact: Useful phrases: «a successful attempt», «be successful in», «highly successful».
fact: «Dyslexia» is a difference that makes reading and spelling harder; the example sentence says it has nothing to do with being clever.
exercise: «A successful experiment gives the result you tested for.» What does successful mean here? | Finished late | Very expensive | *Working as planned | Hard to read
exercise: Mia practised every day and became ____ in her swimming races. Which word fits the gap? | glum | ancient | *successful | curt
exercise: Copy the word from «many very successful people have it» that describes people who did well in life. | spelling | difference | clever | *successful
test: «The team had a successful day.» What does successful mean? | It rained all day | They were very tired | *Their day went well and they achieved their goal | They lost every game
test: «His successful business made him rich.» What does successful mean here? | Being very quiet | *Doing well in business | Being very old | Being sad
exam: Which meaning fits «a successful attempt» best? | *Achieving what you tried to do | Very old | Giving out light | Short and rude
